      "text": "To solve the expression \\(\\frac{3 + 5i}{3 - 5i} + \\frac{3 - 5i}{3 + 5i}\\), we can start by simplifying each fraction separately and then adding the results. The general approach involves multiplying the numerator and the denominator by the complex conjugate of the denominator.\n\nFirst, let's simplify \\(\\frac{3 + 5i}{3 - 5i}\\):\n\n\\[\n\\frac{3 + 5i}{3 - 5i} \\cdot \\frac{3 + 5i}{3 + 5i} = \\frac{(3 + 5i)^2}{(3 - 5i)(3 + 5i)}.\n\\]\n\nThe denominator simplifies as follows:\n\n\\[\n(3 - 5i)(3 + 5i) = 3^2 - (5i)^2 = 9 - 25i^2 = 9 + 25 = 34.\n\\]\n\nThe numerator expands as follows:\n\n\\[\n(3 + 5i)^2 = 3^2 + 2 \\cdot 3 \\cdot 5i + (5i)^2 = 9 + 30i + 25i^2 = 9 + 30i - 25 = -16 + 30i.\n\\]\n\nSo, we have:\n\n\\[\n\\frac{3 + 5i}{3 - 5i} = \\frac{-16 + 30i}{34} = -\\frac{16}{34} + \\frac{30i}{34} = -\\frac{8}{17} + \\frac{15i}{17}.\n\\]\n\nNext, let's simplify \\(\\frac{3 - 5i}{3 + 5i}\\):\n\n\\[\n\\frac{3 - 5i}{3 + 5i} \\cdot \\frac{3 - 5i}{3 - 5i} = \\frac{(3 - 5i)^2}{(3 + 5i)(3 - 5i)}.\n\\]\n\nThe denominator simplifies as follows:\n\n\\[\n(3 + 5i)(3 - 5i) = 3^2 - (5i)^2 = 9 - 25i^2 = 9 + 25 = 34.\n\\]\n\nThe numerator expands as follows:\n\n\\[\n(3 - 5i)^2 = 3^2 - 2 \\cdot 3 \\cdot 5i + (5i)^2 = 9 - 30i + 25i^2 = 9 - 30i - 25 = -16 - 30i.\n\\]\n\nSo, we have:\n\n\\[\n\\frac{3 - 5i}{3 + 5i} = \\frac{-16 - 30i}{34} = -\\frac{16}{34} - \\frac{30i}{34} = -\\frac{8}{17} - \\frac{15i}{17}.\n\\]\n\nNow, we add the two simplified fractions:\n\n\\[\n\\left( -\\frac{8}{17} + \\frac{15i}{17} \\right) + \\left( -\\frac{8}{17} - \\frac{15i}{17} \\right) = -\\frac{8}{17} - \\frac{8}{17} + \\frac{15i}{17} - \\frac{15i}{17} = -\\frac{16}{17} + 0i = -\\frac{16}{17}.\n\\]\n\nTherefore, the final answer is:\n\n\\[\n\\boxed{-\\frac{16}{17}}.\n\\]",
