      "text": "To simplify the expression \\(\\frac{3 + 5i}{3 - 5i} + \\frac{3 - 5i}{3 + 5i}\\), we start by finding a common denominator for the two fractions. The common denominator is \\((3 - 5i)(3 + 5i) = 9 + 25 = 34\\). So, we rewrite the expression with the common denominator:\n\n\\[\n\\frac{(3 + 5i)(3 + 5i)}{34} + \\frac{(3 - 5i)(3 - 5i)}{34} = \\frac{(3 + 5i)^2 + (3 - 5i)^2}{34}.\n\\]\n\nNext, we expand the squares in the numerator:\n\n\\[\n(3 + 5i)^2 = 9 + 30i + 25i^2 = 9 + 30i - 25 = -16 + 30i,\n\\]\n\\[\n(3 - 5i)^2 = 9 - 30i + 25i^2 = 9 - 30i - 25 = -16 - 30i.\n\\]\n\nAdding these two results together, we get:\n\n\\[\n(-16 + 30i) + (-16 - 30i) = -16 - 16 = -32.\n\\]\n\nSo the expression simplifies to:\n\n\\[\n\\frac{-32}{34} = -\\frac{16}{17}.\n\\]\n\nTherefore, the simplified form of the given expression is:\n\n\\[\n\\boxed{-\\frac{16}{17}}.\n\\]",
