      "text": "To simplify the expression \\(\\frac{3 + 5i}{3 - 5i} + \\frac{3 - 5i}{3 + 5i}\\), we can start by finding a common denominator for the two fractions. The common denominator for \\((3 - 5i)\\) and \\((3 + 5i)\\) is \\((3 - 5i)(3 + 5i) = 9 + 25 = 34\\).\n\nFirst, we rewrite each fraction with the common denominator 34:\n\n\\[\n\\frac{3 + 5i}{3 - 5i} = \\frac{(3 + 5i)(3 + 5i)}{34} = \\frac{9 + 30i + 25i^2}{34} = \\frac{9 + 30i - 25}{34} = \\frac{-16 + 30i}{34} = -\\frac{16}{34} + \\frac{30i}{34} = -\\frac{8}{17} + \\frac{15i}{17}\n\\]\n\n\\[\n\\frac{3 - 5i}{3 + 5i} = \\frac{(3 - 5i)(3 - 5i)}{34} = \\frac{9 - 30i + 25i^2}{34} = \\frac{9 - 30i - 25}{34} = \\frac{-16 - 30i}{34} = -\\frac{16}{34} - \\frac{30i}{34} = -\\frac{8}{17} - \\frac{15i}{17}\n\\]\n\nNow, we add the two fractions:\n\n\\[\n\\left( -\\frac{8}{17} + \\frac{15i}{17} \\right) + \\left( -\\frac{8}{17} - \\frac{15i}{17} \\right) = -\\frac{8}{17} - \\frac{8}{17} + \\frac{15i}{17} - \\frac{15i}{17} = -\\frac{16}{17} + 0i = -\\frac{16}{17}\n\\]\n\nThus, the simplified form of the expression is:\n\n\\[\n\\boxed{-\\frac{16}{17}}\n\\]",
